{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And now, pray, take your gear.</b> He specifies here the sword and the bow, for such is the way of one who goes out to the field, that he girds his sword and his bow with which he hunts birds — this is its plain sense; and it alludes as well to his seed, that their weapons of war would be these." "<b>And by way of the Midrash:</b> 'Take your gear' (שא נא כליך) — this is the kingdom of Babylon, as is said (Daniel 1:2): ״ואת הכלים הביא בבלה״; 'you will bring' (תליך) — this is Media, as is said (Esther 7:10): ״ויתלו את המן״; 'and your bow' (וקשתך) — this is Greece, as is said (Zechariah 9:13): ״כי דרכתי לי יהודה קשת״ etc.; 'and go out to the field' (וצא השדה) — this is Edom, as is said (Genesis 32:4): ״ארצה שעיר שדה אדום״." "<b>And hunt game for me.</b> It is written צידה — he commanded him concerning ritual slaughter and warned him against the five things that invalidate a slaughter."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:15:31.994038855Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}